{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2174-01-04 12:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hi, I'm Dr. Lee. I understand you've been having abdominal pain. Can you tell me more about it?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2174-01-04 12:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, it’s on the right side, near my belly and lower abdomen. It started about four days ago and hurts more when I move."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2174-01-04 12:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I see. Is it constant or does it come and go? And how would you rate the pain, on a scale from 1 to 10?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2174-01-04 12:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "It was an 8 at first, but now it’s around a 5. Lying still helps a lot."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2174-01-04 12:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Okay, thanks. You mentioned nausea too. Has that gotten worse?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2174-01-04 12:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "No, it’s about the same. I still take Zofran in the morning like usual."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2174-01-04 12:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good. We’ve reviewed your history. You’ve had gastric bypass and now rely on tube feeds, correct?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2174-01-04 12:07:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, that’s right. After the surgery, I couldn’t keep food down, so I’ve been on tube feeds for a while."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2174-01-04 12:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ve stopped your tube feeds for now and started IV fluids to let your gut rest. We also ordered a CT scan to check for any blockages."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2174-01-04 12:09:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Is there a chance something’s blocked? I’ve been worried about that."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2174-01-04 12:10:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It’s possible, but your symptoms could also be from irritation or bacterial overgrowth. The CT will help us rule out a blockage."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2174-01-04 12:11:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, that makes sense. And my G-tube is still working fine?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2174-01-04 12:12:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, the tube is in place and the site looks clean. We’ll keep monitoring it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2174-01-04 13:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your CT scan is back. Good news — no signs of a blockage in your intestines. The G-tube is where it should be, in the excluded stomach."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2174-01-04 13:31:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s a relief. So what’s causing the pain then?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2174-01-04 13:32:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We think it’s likely due to irritation from the tube feeds or possibly bacterial overgrowth, which you’ve had before."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2174-01-04 13:33:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ve been on rifaximin for that. Should we keep it?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2174-01-04 13:34:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, we’ll continue your rifaximin. We’ll also start adding back your tube feeds slowly tomorrow."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2174-01-04 13:35:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, but what if the pain comes back when we restart them?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2174-01-04 13:36:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll start very low and go slow. If you have any issues, we’ll pause and reassess. Your safety comes first."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2174-01-05 08:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. How’s the pain today?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2174-01-05 08:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "It’s better, maybe a 3 now. I slept okay."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2174-01-05 08:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Great. We’re going to start your tube feeds again at a low rate — 20 cc per hour — and increase slowly."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2174-01-05 08:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay. And what about my nausea?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2174-01-05 08:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll keep your morning Zofran. Let us know if it gets worse."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2174-01-05 10:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ve started your tube feeds at 20 cc/hr. The nurse will monitor you closely."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2174-01-05 10:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I feel a little full, but no pain yet."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2174-01-05 12:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "The enteral nutrition team just confirmed your feeds are infusing well at 20 cc/hr. No issues so far."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 29,
      "time": "2174-01-05 12:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s good. Can we go higher later?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 30,
      "time": "2174-01-05 12:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Possibly. We’ll assess this afternoon. We don’t want to rush it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 31,
      "time": "2174-01-05 15:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your labs came back — all stable. White count is normal, no signs of infection."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 32,
      "time": "2174-01-05 15:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And my liver and kidneys? I’ve had fatty liver before."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 33,
      "time": "2174-01-05 15:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Liver enzymes are normal. Kidney function is excellent. You’re doing well."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 34,
      "time": "2174-01-06 08:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Morning. How are you feeling?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 35,
      "time": "2174-01-06 08:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Pain is down to a 2. Feels like I’m turning a corner."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 36,
      "time": "2174-01-06 08:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s great. We’ve increased your tube feeds to 40 cc/hr and plan to go to 60 by tonight."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 37,
      "time": "2174-01-06 08:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s my usual rate. I hope I can stay on it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 38,
      "time": "2174-01-06 08:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re optimistic. We’re also adding sucralfate to protect your stomach lining and lansoprazole for acid control."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 39,
      "time": "2174-01-06 08:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Is that because of my past ulcers?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 40,
      "time": "2174-01-06 08:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Exactly. It’s preventive. We also added docusate for constipation, which can happen with pain meds."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 41,
      "time": "2174-01-06 14:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ve been on 60 cc/hr for a few hours and tolerating it well. We’re calling that a success."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 42,
      "time": "2174-01-06 14:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s a relief. Does this mean I can go home soon?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 43,
      "time": "2174-01-06 14:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Possibly tomorrow. We’ll make sure your pain is controlled and you’re stable on full feeds."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 44,
      "time": "2174-01-06 14:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ll need help with wound care, right?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 45,
      "time": "2174-01-06 14:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, home health will visit to help with dressing changes. We’ll set that up."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 46,
      "time": "2174-01-07 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good news — you’re being discharged today. Pain is well-controlled, and you’re on full tube feeds."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 47,
      "time": "2174-01-07 09:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s great. What meds am I going home with?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 48,
      "time": "2174-01-07 09:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Rifaximin twice daily, sucralfate three times a day, lansoprazole twice daily, docusate twice daily, and Dilaudid for pain as needed."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 49,
      "time": "2174-01-07 09:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And when should I call or come back?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 50,
      "time": "2174-01-07 09:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "If you have a fever over 101.5, severe pain, vomiting, or redness around the tube site, come back right away."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 51,
      "time": "2174-01-07 09:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Got it. Thank you for taking such good care of me."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 52,
      "time": "2174-01-07 09:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re welcome. We’ll follow up with your surgeon for an appointment. Rest well."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 53,
      "time": "2174-01-07 10:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Just confirming — home health is set for wound care, and your pharmacy has your prescriptions."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 54,
      "time": "2174-01-07 10:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, I got the call. Everything’s arranged."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 55,
      "time": "2174-01-07 10:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Perfect. You’re cleared to go home. Take care and keep in touch."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 56,
      "time": "2174-01-07 10:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you, Dr. Lee. I really appreciate it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 57,
      "time": "2174-01-07 11:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "One last thing — make sure to crush all pills before giving them through the G-tube."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 58,
      "time": "2174-01-07 11:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, I remember from last time. I’ll be careful."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 59,
      "time": "2174-01-07 11:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good. And avoid heavy lifting for now. Let the incision heal."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 60,
      "time": "2174-01-07 11:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Understood. I’ll take it easy."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 61,
      "time": "2174-01-07 12:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re officially discharged. Home health will visit tomorrow. Call us with any concerns."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 62,
      "time": "2174-01-07 12:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you again. I feel much better."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 63,
      "time": "2174-01-07 12:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re glad. Take care and rest well."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 64,
      "time": "2174-01-07 12:30:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Just wanted to say I made it home safely. Everything’s set up."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 65,
      "time": "2174-01-07 12:31:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s wonderful to hear. We’ll check in soon. Rest and recover."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2174-01-04 11:53:00",
    "admission_end": "2174-01-07 13:00:00",
    "summary_paragraph": "The patient was admitted for right-sided abdominal pain and nausea, occurring four days prior to admission. She has a history of gastric bypass and relies on tube feeds due to poor oral intake and post-surgical hypoglycemia. Initial management included NPO status and IV fluids. A CT scan ruled out bowel obstruction, showing the G-tube in correct position without signs of blockage. Tube feeds were restarted gradually and advanced to her baseline rate of 60 cc/hr, which she tolerated well. Pain and nausea were controlled throughout the stay. She was discharged home with home health services for wound care, continuing rifaximin, sucralfate, lansoprazole, docusate, and PRN Dilaudid. Follow-up was arranged with her surgeon.",
    "problems": [
      "Abdominal pain, unspecified site",
      "Nausea alone",
      "Bariatric surgery status",
      "Polycystic ovaries"
    ]
  }
}
